<title>BRAZIL: Brazil opens bids for B Band services in Sao Paulo.</title>
<headline>Brazil opens bids for B Band services in Sao Paulo.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Ministry of Communications Wednesday began opening the bids for concessions to run cellular B Band services in metropolitan Sao Paulo, officials said.</p>
<p>The officials said the winning bid for what is generally regarded as the most attractive of the 10 concession areas up for grabs would be announced during the course of the morning.</p>
<p>The ministry was also due to announce the winner for the Bahia and Sergipe states B Band service area.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-3141193))</p>
